        "id": 1000294
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-05-06T12:03:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This code stops printing at the first error, but the send/receive code collects multiple errors and returns them.\n\nSo I wonder what purpose there is for a transaction that partially succeeds? I guess it makes some sense to support this in the protocol.\n\nBut do we really want to continue on with later segments when an earlier segment fails?\n\nAnother option is:\n\n1. Stop on first error, don\u0027t try to send more segments\n2. Return error information and the segment number where it occurred\n\nThat way presumably both the pass-through code and this response parsing code become simpler, but there doesn\u0027t seem to be any down side.",
      "revId": "12290092685a9fa783771a95dadaa944e59d5ae2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
